From dc8f02ce46c186ec5bc59b8e65e67367dc290992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefano Borghini <projects@stefanoborghinidesign.it>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: rebuild become-a-partner as a step-by-step wizard

Drops the marketing-page layout (pricing showcase, FAQ, process
sections) in favor of a single step-by-step form, same interaction
pattern and visual language as craft-your-experience: back/progress/
counter header, slide transitions, one focus per screen.

Step 1 asks the operator type (hotel, restaurant, private charter,
tour operator, other); step 3's questions branch on that choice
(DETAIL_FIELDS) instead of asking one generic set. Plan interest
becomes a step with short taglines instead of a public pricing
page. Backend follow-up: partner_applications now stores a single
category plus a flexible details jsonb blob instead of a categories
array, matching the new shape.

Verified interactively end-to-end (category selection -> conditional
step 3 -> plan -> message/submit), including Next-button validation
gating at each step and two real overflow bugs caught and fixed
(flex/grid children need min-w-0 to shrink, not just break-words).
